## What is allowed

You may view this repository and cite the report and the lab notebook. A citation should name the authors and point to this repository.

Any other use of the original materials needs prior permission from the authors. That includes copying the original code into another project, redistributing it, and commercial use.

## Research disclaimer

This software and these documents are a research record of completed experiments. They are not a medical device. They have not been cleared or approved for diagnosis, treatment, or any other clinical use.

Model outputs, simulated dialogues, scores, and notebook tables are experimental measurements. They are not medical advice and must not be used to make decisions about a patient. The authors and their institution accept no liability for use of this repository.

THE ORIGINAL MATERIALS ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.

## Third-party materials

These components keep the licenses chosen by their own authors. Nothing in this file relicenses them.

- `src/` is the MediQ benchmark from https://github.com/stellalisy/mediQ. The MediQ code and the iMEDQA cases used here are under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY 4.0). Attribution to the MediQ authors is required for those materials.
- `data/all_mediq_craft_merged.jsonl` mixes MediQ cases with CRAFT-MD cases. CRAFT-MD remains under its upstream terms.
- AI Hospital and 3MDBench cases used by `clinic_experiment/` remain under their upstream terms. The checked-in code that runs those experiments is original material. Copies of upstream patient records, if present, are not.
- MedRAG textbook passages were used to build local retrieval indexes. Those indexes are not part of this repository. The textbooks, including any StatPearls content, remain under their publishers' terms.
- Model weights (including Llama and Qwen mirrors) are not included. Use of those weights is governed by the model maker's license.

